1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,170
ADAM MCP connects your University of Basel courses to an MCP-compatible assistant. Here
is one study workflow, illustrated with synthetic course data.

2
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:22,900
Sign in through a dedicated Chrome session. Ask for your courses, then choose the one
you want to explore. Course links take you back to ADAM.

3
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:36,750
Ask for available deadlines in that course. Results cite their source. If a listing is
incomplete, the assistant should say so. An empty folder does not mean there are no
deadlines.

4
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:48,560
Search your enrolled course tree for a topic, such as Fourier transforms. Search covers
titles and available page text. It is not ADAM's global search.

5
00:00:48,560 --> 00:01:03,538
Select a page and approve the read. Page text, file extracts, exercise instructions, and
forum posts require approval for the selected object. Declining returns no body text.

6
00:01:03,538 --> 00:01:16,956
The assistant can work with the approved text and cite its ADAM link. Extracts are
bounded. Scanned PDFs have no OCR, and mathematical notation may need checking in the
original.

7
00:01:16,956 --> 00:01:32,606
The server runs on your machine. Sign-in stays in Chrome. Returned text goes to the
model provider chosen in your client. Exams, grades, submissions, and other writes are
unsupported.

8
00:01:32,606 --> 00:01:47,272
Explore the setup guide and client compatibility notes in the repository. ADAM MCP is an
unofficial, open-source community project. This illustration does not certify a client
integration.
